# Schedule Interview Dialog

The recruiter's booking form for one interview round. They choose the interviewers, a day and a round type, and the slot row shows which hourly slots (9:00–17:00) are still free for **every** chosen interviewer, computed from the meetings the caller passes in.

```hbs
<ScheduleInterviewDialog
  @candidate={{this.candidate}}
  @employees={{this.employees}}
  @meetings={{this.meetings}}
  @isRunning={{this.scheduling}}
  @error={{this.scheduleError}}
  @onConfirm={{this.schedule}}
  @onCancel={{this.closeSchedule}}
/>
```

```ts
import { ScheduleInterviewDialog } from '@cardstack/catalog/cards/hr/components/schedule-interview-dialog';
```

Slots are one hour, the length Schedule Interview books, so a slot shown free is exactly the interval the command re-checks. When the command still finds a clash, its error shows in the dialog with a deliberate "book anyway" override, passed back as `ignoreConflicts`.

### Non-goals

No calendar sync with outside calendars. No time zones beyond the viewer's own.
